@* The host page. The five library asset lines below are the block in
   docs/getting-started.md, in that order, with catalogue.css standing in for the
   app's own brand.css. HostPageTests asserts the two agree — so the block every
   consuming app copies is executed on every CI run rather than merely scanned.

   Plain _content/Sedna.UI/… hrefs, deliberately not @@Assets[…]: a
   fingerprinted URL would make the page that documents the load order differ from
   the page anyone can paste. *@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover" />

    @* Before every relative URL below, or it does not apply to them. Without it a
       browser resolves them against the current path rather than the root, so a
       direct hit on a sub-route asks for its assets under that route and gets a 404
       — the page renders unstyled and never becomes interactive, and only on a
       direct hit, never when the router navigated there. *@
    <base href="/" />

    <script src="_content/Sedna.UI/js/Sedna.UI.boot.js"></script>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/Sedna.UI/lib/remixicon/remixicon.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/Sedna.UI/css/Sedna.UI.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="catalogue.css" />

    <link rel="icon" href="favicon.ico" />

    @* Forest and Cobalt's palettes, so the Branding page's live switcher has more
       than one to move between. Sedna's own needs no block here — it already ships
       as literals in Sedna.UI.css — so this is invisible until that page's switch
       is used. *@
    <SednaBrandStyle />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>
<body>
    @* Blazor's reconnect UI, in the library's own status-bar classes. Supply it or the
       framework injects its default one — a white box with inline styles, in an app
       that has a theme. This block is Examples/StatusBar/HostPage.html verbatim,
       and HostPageTests compares the two, so the markup on the Shell & nav page is the
       markup this site actually runs. *@
    <div id="components-reconnect-modal">
        <div class="status-bar status-bar--reconnecting">
            <i class="ri-wifi-off-line"></i>
            <span>
                Connection lost. Reconnecting…
                @* Blazor fills these two by id, if they are there. *@
                <span class="status-bar-attempt">
                    attempt <span id="components-reconnect-current-attempt">1</span>
                    of <span id="components-reconnect-max-retries">8</span>
                </span>
            </span>
        </div>
        <div class="status-bar status-bar--paused">
            <i class="ri-pause-circle-line"></i>
            <span>Paused. Your work is held on the server.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="status-bar status-bar--failed">
            <i class="ri-close-circle-line"></i><span>Could not reconnect.</span>
            <button class="status-bar-action" type="button" onclick="location.reload()">
                <i class="ri-refresh-line"></i> Retry
            </button>
        </div>
        <div class="status-bar status-bar--expired">
            <i class="ri-error-warning-line"></i><span>This session has expired on the server.</span>
            <button class="status-bar-action" type="button" onclick="location.reload()">
                <i class="ri-refresh-line"></i> Reload
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* The same family's other mount: Blazor's unhandled-error bar, which the framework
       reveals with an inline `display: block`. The id is the container and the strip is
       the child — see Examples/StatusBar/ErrorBarHostPage.html, which this block is. *@
    <div id="blazor-error-ui">
        <div class="status-bar status-bar--error">
            <i class="ri-alert-line"></i>
            <span>An unhandled error has occurred.</span>
            <button class="status-bar-action" type="button" onclick="location.reload()">
                <i class="ri-refresh-line"></i> Reload
            </button>
            <button class="status-bar-dismiss" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss this message"
                    onclick="this.closest('#blazor-error-ui').style.display='none'">
                <i class="ri-close-line"></i>
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* Global interactivity. The invariant: every example demo and every code block
       renders identically before the circuit connects — interactivity adds
       behaviour, it is never required to see an example. *@
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />

    @* Sedna.UI.js before blazor.web.js, so window.sednaUi exists before an
       interactive component can call into it. *@
    <script src="_content/Sedna.UI/js/Sedna.UI.js"></script>
    <script src="catalogue.js"></script>
    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
